  "id": "nucleus-accumbens",
  "term": "nucleus accumbens",
  "definition": "The nucleus accumbens is a group of variably shaped nerve cells located near the front lower part of the lateral ventricle, in the area of the olfactory tubercle between the head of the caudate nucleus and the anterior perforated substance. It is considered part of the ventral striatum within the basal ganglia.",
